WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.180
Wow, Mom's pretty!

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:10.530
This is amazing, amazing!
I wanna get married too!

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.280
Isn't this great, Ai?

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.590
Your mom is really pretty.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.790
Who are you again?

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:20.460
What's wrong, Ai?

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.660
Hey, Miho. I forgot who is this?

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.160
Who are you talking to, Hasebe?

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:27.440
Fujiwara, do you know her?

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.510
Hey, you! What's your name again?

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.010
I've never seen her before, have you?

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:34.310
But why?

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:35.640
Hey, Yuu!

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.950
Do you know who this girl is?

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:39.820
Huh?

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.390
Yuu, it's me!

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:43.900
Who are you?

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:46.180
Yuu?

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.760
What is it, Haruka?

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:52.660
What?

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.100
Ugh, she's spacing out again!

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.740
I...

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:02.070
I think I was having a weird dream.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.600
You can dream while you're walking?

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.410
That's our Haruka.

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:08.380
That dream...

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:11.480
Wasn't it a hallucination that
everyone had forgotten who you were?

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:15.450
But are you actually here right now?

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:20.140
Or can this dimension
be only an illusion?

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:24.700
Perhaps you are just lost in a dream...

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:27.330
of a phantom dimension.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.670
Think about it, Haruka.

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:31.950
The wedding of Ai's mother and father...

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:34.590
really happened yesterday, didn't it?

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.430
I was there too, wasn't I?

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:41.700
Come on, this can't
be just a dream, right?

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.320
Oh, I know!

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:53.080
Found it!

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:58.670
I really do exist

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.550
...since I was little.

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:04.180
Whoa...

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:11.860
Wow, there's so many pictures
of me when I was really tiny.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:19.940
There's more, aren't there?

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:22.950
Huh?

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:29.170
This is a video tape, right?

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.110
A magnetic tape.
Haven't seen these in a while.

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:36.810
Hey, Tobi? How come I can't
watch it on our video deck.

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:38.350
Do you know why?

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.250
The deck probably uses
a different standard.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.990
How can I watch it?

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:44.460
Well...

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:47.050
Is something important recorded on it?

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:50.140
It should have footage of me
from when I was little.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.700
I'd like to see that too.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.390
Can I watch it with you, Haruka?

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:57.480
Of course, Atori!

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:00.310
Hey, Tobi? What should I do?

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:04.550
The quickest way is to find
a deck that can play this tape.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.030
This is an 8 millimeter video.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:13.180
And I don't have
a deck that can play it.

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:16.060
Hey, Yuu? Do you know anyone
that would have one?

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:19.420
It's a pretty old machine.

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:23.030
Why do you want to watch
an old video all of a sudden?

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:26.810
It's kind of hard to explain.

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:30.680
But I want to watch it.
I have to watch it!

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:32.680
Weirdo.

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:34.880
Why don't we ask Isami?

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:37.410
Maybe his brother Tsuyoshi
knows where we can find one.

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:15.580
Damn! Damn! Damn!

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:17.580
Damn!

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:27.360
Betrayed again? You poor guy.

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:32.870
Your destiny is inevitably unfortunate.

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:35.580
I pity you, Kuina.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:38.170
Noein?! Please...

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:41.130
Please take me away
to Shangri-la, quickly!

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:44.050
That I cannot do.

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:48.050
You have yet to fulfill
your part of the bargain.

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:51.550
The Dragon Torque is increasing
its power! It won't be easy...

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:57.150
Its power accelerated...

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:59.760
thanks to its contact with La'cryma.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:02.530
More than I had predicted it would.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.770
With that much power...

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:10.180
it can come to Shangri-la
of its own free will.

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:14.010
I've lost faith in you, Kuina...

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:17.280
...and I came all the way to La'cryma...

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:19.750
to grant your request.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:21.950
W... Wait...

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:24.460
You have completed your duty.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:25.550
I...

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:27.580
This is goodbye, Kuina.

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:29.390
Please wait, Noein!

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:32.730
Take me to Shangri-la!
Take me to Shangri-la, please!

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:34.770
Please...

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:37.000
Please don't leave me here!

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:42.900
An 8 millimeter video, huh?

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:46.490
Does anyone still use those anymore?

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:49.670
I thought maybe there
would be one at your house.

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:51.780
Since you're rich
and have tons of stuff!

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:55.720
Non, non! The rich discard the old...

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:57.660
and buy the new.

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:02.040
The only thing that the rich treasure
forever is cold, hard cash.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:02.050
Hey...
The only thing that the rich treasure
forever is cold, hard cash.

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:03.120
Hey...

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:05.930
In an emergency,
cash always wins hands-down.

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:07.590
That's true.

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:08.630
Haruka!

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:12.470
I know! Maybe that's
a "cursed video tape"!

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:13.030
Huh?

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:15.300
Like if you don't watch it, you'll die.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:18.680
That's it! It might be a cursed video tape
that will kill if someone else watches it!

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:21.370
- Where is Goto looking?
- Scary, scary!

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:24.560
- He's asking at Fujiwara's.
- Fujiwara?!

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:28.150
What's this? That's an awfully
cute reaction towards Fujiwara-kun.

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:31.780
Y-You're wrong!
Why would I react towards him?

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:34.760
Oh, oh! Your anger is verrry suspicious.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:36.660
Miho!

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.870
I swear I will get to Shangri-la!

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:56.220
Are you gonna ask the girl directly?

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:01.430
That's the fastest way to get
in contact with Dr. Mayuzumi, isn't it?

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:04.780
Well, yeah, but don't you think
the professor will become wary...

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:06.760
if you get his kid involved?

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:11.860
Get her involved? Haruka-chan may
be at the center of this incident.

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:15.000
I still can't believe it...

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:17.570
...with this alternate dimension and all...

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:22.400
I keep thinking that we're just
having the same long nightmare.

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:26.740
There you are.

00:09:26.780 --> 00:09:28.580
What'cha doing?

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:29.950
Looking at the sea.

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:31.040
The sea?

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:34.380
There was no sea where I lived.

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:36.990
Oh.

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:39.190
You don't have to try to remember.

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:41.960
Let the unpleasant things stay forgotten.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:45.060
Yeah. But...

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:47.310
I'm still worried about Sara.

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:49.320
Atori...

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.230
Good afternoon!
Is Haruka-chan around?

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:56.610
Uchida-san! I think
she's out at the moment.

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:58.940
Let's wait for her inside.

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:00.880
Hey, Uchida-chan...

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:10.820
What are you doing?
I know you're there.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:15.620
I'm looking at you.

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:17.150
I told you.

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:20.470
I plan to be there to see
you vanish in this dimension.

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:25.900
Behave yourself until you
synchronize to this dimension.

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:28.810
Karasu?

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:37.310
So, you left to be with Karasu.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:41.310
I didn't think you
would betray me as well.

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:43.020
Kuina...

00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:45.680
So, you care for him so much...

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:48.710
...you decided to disappear
at his side in this dimension.

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:52.520
Why don't you understand?!

00:10:52.570 --> 00:10:56.590
Every dimension in existence
only gives grief to the living!

00:10:58.010 --> 00:11:00.570
Think of your own past.

00:11:00.610 --> 00:11:03.890
Wasn't it filled with
darkness and despair!

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:10.600
Shangri-la is trying to
straighten out that warp.

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:12.650
You've sided with Shangri-la?!

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:16.360
Go to Shangri-la and you will
be freed from all suffering.

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:18.240
Traitor!

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:33.200
Use this so that you can
survive as long as possible.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:43.070
We came to this dimension
to capture the Dragon Torque.

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:43.760
What?

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:46.320
Dragon Torque? What's that?

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:50.120
I think I should tell you
everything there is to know.

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:52.990
Dragon Torque is our codename...

00:11:53.030 --> 00:11:55.590
for the aggregate of
high density REIZU particles.

00:11:55.630 --> 00:11:59.860
REIZU particles? What did
you try to do with it?

00:12:00.730 --> 00:12:03.830
Our dimension is on
the verge of obliteration.

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:08.470
The contact with a dimension,
we call Shangri-la, is the cause.

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:10.930
We use the particles
to hold the destruction.

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:13.240
Dimensions being obliterated...

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:15.090
...and you found it?

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:17.470
Sort of, but...

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:20.980
What? Let's not start
keeping secrets now.

00:12:21.690 --> 00:12:26.890
You're right. The quantum computer in
our world estimated the coordinates...

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:29.900
and quantized humans
like us has observed...

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:33.480
and confirmed the existence
in the simulated dimension.

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:38.470
The first one who found
the Dragon Torque was Karasu...

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:42.200
who was coincidentally flung into
the dimensional ravine in mid-combat.

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:45.990
Hold on a sec! Don't tell me
that your Dragon Torque is...

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:48.910
To us, this world
was just a coordinate...

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:51.710
calculated by the quantum computer...

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:53.950
and it was supposed to be only
a world made of imaginary numbers.

00:12:53.990 --> 00:12:57.710
The skies, the earth...
it's only an illusion to us.

00:12:58.390 --> 00:13:02.730
So the Dragon Torque
was suppose to be... but...

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:06.820
But the moment you guys wandered
into this world of imaginary numbers...

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:09.360
this world became real...

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:12.720
And Haruka as well in the form
of a 12 year old girl.

00:13:17.680 --> 00:13:22.510
Your world is only one
of many possible futures...

00:13:22.550 --> 00:13:26.950
but if the causes that made that future
is starting to occur in this world...

00:13:27.190 --> 00:13:30.320
Wait a minute, Uchida-san.
From your point of view...

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:33.490
the future is a world
expressed by an imaginary number.

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:35.620
It's not possible for the future...

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:38.580
to be influenced by this world
which is the reality.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:42.360
But the Magic Circle Project
is about to start an experiment...

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:46.200
of how to artificially create
what your world calls it...

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:48.230
the REIZU particles.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:53.640
That's not good. The violation
of causation is being realized...

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:56.310
through Shangri-la's
dimensional erasure.

00:13:56.680 --> 00:14:00.110
This world is starting to
be influenced by the future?

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:06.450
The ocean...

00:14:07.130 --> 00:14:08.820
The ocean is shining?!

00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:15.660
You have good moves despite
being severed from the pipeline.

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:19.370
You were a good dragon soldier.
It's a shame.

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:23.270
In your current state,
I alone can defeat you!

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:27.540
Disappear!

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:49.700
Not bad, Karasu!

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:17.100
Sh... Shangri-la!

00:15:17.630 --> 00:15:20.230
Big bro says he borrowed it
from a friend of his.

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:22.900
Aren't you glad you
found a video deck, Haruka?

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:23.700
Uh-huh.

00:15:23.740 --> 00:15:26.870
Now we can find out the truth
behind the cursed video tape!

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:27.990
Get with it!

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:30.070
You could just watch it at my house...

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:33.170
She doesn't want us watching
her embarrassing childhood videos.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:35.080
That's not the reason, but...

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:38.580
If it's a video of memories,
you should watch it by yourself.

00:15:39.690 --> 00:15:41.050
Haruka...

00:15:42.220 --> 00:15:43.420
Who's there?

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:45.500
I'm coming for you.

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:49.350
What's wrong, Haruka?

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:00.570
I don't like this wind.

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:01.940
Something's coming.

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:03.570
Haruka...

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:05.870
There it is.

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:08.400
Shangri-la?

00:16:57.370 --> 00:16:59.090
Search-and-assault ships!

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:04.710
Kuina?!

00:17:10.610 --> 00:17:12.670
Hey, what do you think that is?

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:14.680
It's not a plane, is it?

00:17:14.710 --> 00:17:17.740
Doesn't look like one.
That's not what it is...

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:20.520
Then what is it?

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:23.270
It's Shangri-la.

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:26.890
What the heck is that?!
How can something like that fly?!

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:31.460
Are you saying that
came from the future too?!

00:17:31.970 --> 00:17:33.110
Well, Tobi?

00:17:33.430 --> 00:17:36.610
We call that Shangri-la
search-and-assault ship.

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:40.950
It's a weapon used to overlap
dimensions with Shangri-La.

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:44.670
Hey, that's not funny.
What on earth is going to happen?!

00:17:45.110 --> 00:17:48.240
That will be used to assimilate
this region into Shangri-la.

00:17:49.220 --> 00:17:50.510
What's it doing here?

00:17:50.550 --> 00:17:52.780
Don't tell me it's after Haruka-chan...

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:57.470
I know that. I know what that is.

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:00.720
Shangri-la...

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:04.350
Atori?! Are you okay, Atori?!

00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:29.710
It's way too fake!
That has to be a mirage!

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:32.490
Do mirages usually
have that much detail?

00:18:32.530 --> 00:18:36.660
It's fake, a fake!
It's nothing but a fake!

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:39.100
Seriously impossible.

00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:40.850
You think that came
from the future too?!

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:41.700
The future?

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:44.000
Why is something like that
coming from the future?!

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:45.700
From the future...

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:49.140
Pull yourself together, Miho!

00:18:52.050 --> 00:18:54.440
D... Dragon Torque...

00:18:55.350 --> 00:18:56.840
Wh-What IS that guy?!

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:58.350
Impossible!

00:19:01.520 --> 00:19:03.450
As long as I have you...

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:04.660
Run for it, Haruka!

00:19:05.190 --> 00:19:06.180
Let go!

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:08.380
Stop it! Let her go, you monster!

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:10.990
What's this?!

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:14.420
Yuu!

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:18.440
Noein! Can you hear me?!
I've secured the Dragon Torque!

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:22.200
Take me... Take me
with you to Shangri-la!

00:19:22.240 --> 00:19:23.730
Noein!

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:27.200
H... Haruka!

00:19:29.450 --> 00:19:30.520
Noein!

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:34.480
Let her go!

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:36.480
It's him...

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:37.740
Karasu!

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:40.990
Karasu! Why you...

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:55.290
I'm going to Shangri-la...

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:20.240
Don't you meddle!

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:25.620
I told you, I no longer have
a need for your pathetic help.

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:29.270
I successfully captured
the Dragon Torque for you!

00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:33.470
You are unnecessary in this dimension.

00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:35.470
Disappear.

00:20:37.590 --> 00:20:39.410
Miserable fool...

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:45.080
So you manipulated Kuina, Noein.

00:20:48.630 --> 00:20:50.560
You erased Fukuro!

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:52.270
You!

00:20:56.610 --> 00:20:58.070
How unfortunate.

00:20:58.100 --> 00:21:02.370
I wanted to bring you
a lot more suffering.

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:08.830
You can also collapse and die.
Look at him.

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:24.550
I will not forgive you.

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:27.600
I'll never, ever forgive you!

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:29.720
Haruka?!

00:21:29.940 --> 00:21:31.630
That's...

00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:51.120
Why, the time is quite ripe indeed.

00:21:59.170 --> 00:22:00.630
Haruka?!

00:22:05.510 --> 00:22:07.050
Are you all right, Haruka?

00:22:07.070 --> 00:22:11.010
Yeah, I'm okay. Thanks, Karasu.

00:22:24.160 --> 00:22:25.720
- What the?
- It's gone.

00:22:25.760 --> 00:22:27.280
They're gone too!

00:22:27.630 --> 00:22:30.030
Where did you go, Haruka?

00:22:31.130 --> 00:22:32.620
Haruka!

00:22:33.600 --> 00:22:36.370
It's okay. Karasu rescued me.

00:22:36.770 --> 00:22:37.870
He did?

00:22:37.870 --> 00:22:40.380
He said to be grateful to you.

00:22:40.380 --> 00:22:41.420
What?

00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:45.440
He said that he was given strength
because you fought for me.

00:22:46.150 --> 00:22:47.310
Because of me?

00:22:47.350 --> 00:22:48.880
There's nothing on it!

00:22:48.880 --> 00:22:52.110
Not on this one, or this one...
They're all gone!

00:22:52.150 --> 00:22:54.390
The shot I got of that guy
...it's not there!

00:22:54.650 --> 00:22:57.120
How come?! Why isn't he showing up?!

00:22:57.160 --> 00:22:58.750
I don't know!

00:22:59.690 --> 00:23:02.180
Were we just dreaming?

00:23:03.600 --> 00:23:04.520
No.

00:23:05.670 --> 00:23:07.720
We saw him.

00:24:42.300 --> 00:24:44.260
I'm dreaming again.

00:24:45.230 --> 00:24:47.100
That summer day's dream.

00:24:48.170 --> 00:24:50.600
I remember it.

00:24:53.510 --> 00:24:55.590
I will perform
a fixed reverse calculation.

00:24:59.810 --> 00:25:03.440
Even if we are killed,
we can ignore it if we have to.

00:25:03.780 --> 00:25:05.770
Next episode, Memories.

00:25:06.620 --> 00:25:10.400
Can you keep a happy memory
with you forever?
